        "original_id": "9fb30ca5-6f07-5b99-b5d1-15bd655d4991",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: NASA Astronaut Group 15, Producers Guild of America\n- People: Garry Marshall, J. F. Lawton, Julia Roberts, Nick Clooney, Michael Douglas, Robert Guillaume, James Earl Jones, Jack Lemmon, Shirley MacLaine, Walter Matthau, Ronald Reagan, Marlo Thomas, Grant Tinker, Ted Turner\n- Products: Pretty Woman\n- Concepts: The Flying Escargot\n\nFacts:\n- Pretty Woman is a 1990 American romantic comedy film directed by Garry Marshall from a screenplay by J. F. Lawton.\n- Julia Roberts became a Hollywood star after headlining Pretty Woman, which grossed US $464 million worldwide.\n- NASA Astronaut Group 15 adopted “The Flying Escargot” as its moniker, possibly referencing that two group members were from France or the “flying escargot” scene in Pretty Woman.\n- The Producers Guild of America Award ceremony has been hosted each year by celebrity host-presenters including Nick Clooney, Michael Douglas, Robert Guillaume, James Earl Jones, Jack Lemmon, Shirley MacLaine, Garry Marshall, Walter Matthau, Ronald Reagan, Marlo Thomas, Grant Tinker, and Ted Turner.",
